{
 "_frame": "metres; nose -Z (the flying direction), up +Y, right +X; origin = the bounding-box centre (as drones.json): fly the origin along the air lane. Each GLB is one mesh, one material (base colour, normal, metal/rough, emissive; WebP, meshopt). yaw = extra rotation about +Y at load: 0 for every model here (pack_yaw = the turn the pack already gave the raw Tripo mesh); with the track frame: makeBasis(right, up, -tangent), as the racers; an oncoming drone turns 180 deg. size = the full bounds; box = the collision box (w, h, l; x, y, z = its centre in the model frame). rotor_kind + rotors as drones.json: hub centre on the duct rim (duct) or the motor-pod top (open), r = blur disc radius, spin +1 = counter-clockwise seen from above. No rotor discs in the models: open rotors have bare motor pods (no blades), ducts hold Tripo's static fan; draw the spinning blur over them (img/fx/rotor-blur, fan-blur, as src/drone/model.js). lights: kind nav = steady position lamps (side left = red on -x, side right = green on +x), kind strobe = white anti-collision flashes (aviation: about one flash per second, 50-100 ms; never steady); x, y, z = the lamp centre on the surface, w x h = its size in metres, face = the way it points (-x / +x / +y / -y / -z / +z), color = the lens texels' own colour. rule: true = no lens texels of that colour there (Tripo copied the one side the plate showed, or a strobe placed by geometry): draw its sprite. Nav lenses with rule false also glow in the emissive map (factor 1; a lens Tripo copied in the other side's colour is hue-shifted to its own side's colour, Tripo's shading kept: civil_anchors.py --recolor); strobes never do. lights are in glare order (src/traffic/view.js glows the first 4 only): the outermost red, the outermost green, the strobes, then the other lenses. shadow = whether the type casts the sun's shadow on tiers with shadows (only the air taxi: draw-call and triangle budget). Models: Higgsfield Tripo H3.1 (lanes A2 and W4-ART, round 3), anchors measured by tools/art/civil_anchors.py.",
